# Your stomach growls. Grandpa Park asks if you have money and points you to the shop and the snack stall.
# Each <id>-alt<n> is a written wrong reply, using only words met by then; <id>-alt<n>-answer is the answer to it.

hungry = 배고파요?
hungry-reply = 네, 배고파요.

food = 빵 있어요?
food-reply = 아니요, 없어요.

money = 돈 있어요?
money-reply = 네, 있어요.

shop = 가게에 빵이 있어요.
shop-reply = 좋아요!

stall = 가게는 저기, 분식집은 저기.
stall-reply = 감사합니다, 할아버지.
stall-alt1 = 가게예요?

go = 가세요, 가세요!
go-reply = 네. 안녕히 계세요.
go-alt1 = 안녕히 가세요.
